{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CONFIRMED mechanism (outbound_mutation_builders.py:_compute_outbound_update_mutation, ~L203): for a jira_key PRESENT in the fetcher's JQL-search snapshot, jira_fields = jira_snapshot[jira_key] (STALE); the bounded direct GET (_safe_get_issue) is taken ONLY for bound-but-ABSENT keys (bug 1e08 membership-not-value seam). So a just-pushed description re-diffs vs the stale snapshot -> churn until the DC Lucene index catches up (unbounded on the ephemeral harness) -> the test's echo-safety search-wait times out. Investigating 3 resolutions (product confirm-before-push / harness sync-indexing / test relaxation) with history + product-path + harness agents before choosing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787825676287108001,"uuid":"0797ef7d-e3ee-43b5-9a9e-0edd914b4b1a"}